/*
  SRM AP SMART NOTICE BOARD - ESP32 + SUPABASE
  ------------------------------------------------------------
  What this sketch does:
  - Serves Login, Admin Dashboard and Public Notice Board pages from ESP32.
  - Uses Supabase Auth (email/password) in the browser for admin sign-in.
  - Reads/writes notices through the Supabase REST API from the browser.
  - ESP32 polls Supabase and prints the latest notice to Serial Monitor.

  IMPORTANT:
  1) The ESP32-hosted pages work only on the same Wi-Fi/LAN (or its hotspot).
  2) For public access from ANY network, deploy the same HTML pages to a public
     host (e.g. Netlify/Vercel) and use the same Supabase project settings.
  3) NEVER put a Supabase service_role key in this sketch or browser code.
  4) Enable RLS on public.notices. Permit public SELECT; permit INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE
     only for authenticated users (and ideally only an admin role).
  5) Install ArduinoJson library from Library Manager.
  6) Browser email check is only a convenience; enforce admin-only writes with RLS.
  7) Fill in your own Wi-Fi credentials before uploading.
*/

